00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.001
- [Voiceover] Glenn
asks, "Can you elaborate

00:03:42.001 --> 00:03:45.738
"on what the middle is and why it sucks?"

00:03:45.738 --> 00:03:48.085
- Glenn, this is a great question.

00:03:48.085 --> 00:03:50.499
You know, to me the middle
is the commodity work

00:03:50.499 --> 00:03:53.146
and thinking that everybody else does.

00:03:53.146 --> 00:03:56.163
Meaning, it's what the
market's doing right now.

00:03:56.163 --> 00:03:58.787
Like, it's when start-ups pitch me,

00:03:58.787 --> 00:04:01.830
"We're gonna do something
in the photo app space."

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.153
You mean like everybody's been doing

00:04:03.153 --> 00:04:04.430
for the last five years?

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.729
It's commodity work, ya know?

00:04:06.729 --> 00:04:08.703
I think if you're not
trying to break things,

00:04:08.703 --> 00:04:09.655
you're not doing a good job,

00:04:09.655 --> 00:04:12.246
or back to clouds and dirt, non-middle,

00:04:12.256 --> 00:04:14.299
if you're not doing like,
you know what's so funny?

00:04:14.299 --> 00:04:15.854
I've sat through four pitches today,

00:04:15.854 --> 00:04:18.778
and I've liked two, and one is because

00:04:18.778 --> 00:04:21.680
the two guys are just doing the work.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.423
They're like in the weeds.

00:04:23.423 --> 00:04:26.236
They're not doing the big
holistic branding thinking

00:04:26.236 --> 00:04:27.046
game-changing stuff.

00:04:27.046 --> 00:04:29.546
They're just executing,
but at a raw level.

00:04:29.546 --> 00:04:31.713
I just find that there's not that many

00:04:31.713 --> 00:04:35.938
hardcore practitioners,
and there's even less big

00:04:35.938 --> 00:04:38.005
where's the world going, ya know,

00:04:38.005 --> 00:04:40.326
one of those trends at the highest level

00:04:40.326 --> 00:04:42.927
where am I doing the kind of
things at the highest level,

00:04:42.927 --> 00:04:45.825
and so I don't really know
how to explain the work

00:04:45.825 --> 00:04:47.454
but you're surrounded, I'm sorry,

00:04:47.454 --> 00:04:48.987
I don't really know how
to explain the middle,

00:04:48.987 --> 00:04:53.237
but you're surrounded by
it 99.9% of your life.

00:04:53.237 --> 00:04:55.791
- Hey Gary, I have a question
for you for #AskGaryVee.

00:04:55.791 --> 00:04:57.623
- Who cares about that question, Gary.

00:04:57.623 --> 00:04:59.389
This is a more important question.

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:02.594
How are you, if you were the
owner of the New York Jets,

00:05:02.594 --> 00:05:03.824
gonna turn around this team

00:05:03.824 --> 00:05:05.797
and make us a Super Bowl contender?

00:05:05.797 --> 00:05:07.563
Because we both know
that's all that matters,

00:05:07.563 --> 00:05:08.515
and he's a Giants fan.

00:05:08.515 --> 00:05:11.765
Who gives a shit what he has to say?

00:05:11.765 --> 00:05:14.214
- Go Giants.

00:05:14.214 --> 00:05:18.035
- Thanks Brad and
Scooter for the question.

00:05:18.035 --> 00:05:21.325
Ya know, I mean the true
answer to the question,

00:05:21.325 --> 00:05:23.758
'cause I love, you know,
we've decided to go straight

00:05:23.758 --> 00:05:24.837
on this show.

00:05:24.837 --> 00:05:26.718
The true answer is, I'd go in and audit.

00:05:26.718 --> 00:05:27.460
That's what I'd do.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.572
So, as close as I am working
with the Jets as a client,

00:05:30.572 --> 00:05:33.529
watching every play, staying on top of it,

00:05:33.529 --> 00:05:35.913
there's still nuances that
are just not, you know,

00:05:35.913 --> 00:05:37.144
known to me.

00:05:37.144 --> 00:05:39.070
You know, I think one thing
I would do, for example,

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.462
if I bought the Jets today,
I would mandate from the top,

00:05:41.462 --> 00:05:43.877
and this would probably make
it a little harder to get a GM,

00:05:43.877 --> 00:05:45.642
and so that's something
I'd have to quantify,

00:05:45.642 --> 00:05:49.241
but I would mandate that
we draft a quarterback

00:05:49.241 --> 00:05:53.861
every two years in the first
two rounds of the NFL draft

00:05:53.861 --> 00:05:57.182
until we had our guy, right?

00:05:57.182 --> 00:05:59.805
So like I think it's a quarterback league.

00:05:59.805 --> 00:06:00.919
The rules go in that way,

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:02.544
and you have to reverse
engineer to the league,

00:06:02.544 --> 00:06:04.612
and so, for example, right now
I would draft a quarterback

00:06:04.612 --> 00:06:06.962
in round one or two this year because,

00:06:06.962 --> 00:06:08.489
though I've given Gino
the benefit of the doubt,

00:06:08.489 --> 00:06:10.300
he's clearly not the overwhelming

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.204
this is Andrew Luck sitting in our pocket.

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:13.735
So, we have to draft another quarterback,

00:06:13.735 --> 00:06:16.570
and if it's not politically
correct to Gino and his agents

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.007
or to the New York media or the fan base,

00:06:19.007 --> 00:06:21.422
I wouldn't care because I
would dictate to victory

00:06:21.422 --> 00:06:24.069
and I think that's the right
strategy right now in the NFL.

00:06:24.069 --> 00:06:26.393
If you do not have a
quarterback first two rounds,

00:06:26.393 --> 00:06:27.250
you draft one.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.177
You bring 'em in, if you
don't feel good about,

00:06:29.177 --> 00:06:32.102
I'd give it 24 months,
but after full 24 months,

00:06:32.102 --> 00:06:33.913
after a second season of that player,

00:06:33.913 --> 00:06:36.758
by the way, whether he
played a snap or not,

00:06:36.758 --> 00:06:40.340
I would draft another one and
another one and another one

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.983
until I had one because
that is the lynchpin.

00:06:42.983 --> 00:06:44.525
I'd also work on the PR team.

00:06:44.525 --> 00:06:48.473
I would do a weekly show, livestream show

00:06:48.473 --> 00:06:49.984
with the fan base so they could pound me

00:06:49.984 --> 00:06:52.690
with all their angers,
and I'd pound them back

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.865
'cause that's the kind of owner I'd be.

00:06:54.865 --> 00:06:55.763
I would do a bunch of marketing things,

00:06:55.763 --> 00:06:56.598
you've heard me in the past.

00:06:56.598 --> 00:06:59.014
I'd send a jersey of a Jets
jersey to every six-year-old

00:06:59.014 --> 00:07:02.662
in the tri-state area
on their sixth birthday.

00:07:02.662 --> 00:07:04.750
I would probably do a ton
of inappropriate things

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.086
at this point there's, ya know, like

00:07:07.086 --> 00:07:08.836
get into it with the
media because they think

00:07:08.836 --> 00:07:10.322
they're out of their mind with the way

00:07:10.322 --> 00:07:15.332
they're handling the
Jets in this Giants city.

00:07:15.337 --> 00:07:19.384
I would like watch the
game from the stands

00:07:19.384 --> 00:07:21.839
which I think would be
an interesting new thing,

00:07:21.839 --> 00:07:24.183
but that would be tough
because I'd curse at opponents,

00:07:24.183 --> 00:07:26.111
and the NFL would try to reel me in.

00:07:26.111 --> 00:07:29.229
So those are some of
the things I'd be doing.

00:07:29.229 --> 00:07:31.705
